    "done_when": "after promote, reckon fleet-node migrate --session NAME cuts that zellij session over: it ends the session on the old node through a step in the old job, asks the promoted supervisor to start it from ~/.config/zellij/layouts/migrate-NAME.kdl through the shared request writer, then checks each Claude pane the census recorded for that session is a Claude process on the new node with the same conversation id, and records the session's outcome in the ledger; cutover refuses a session the census does not name, skips one already cut over, and without --session names the sessions still to move; once every session has moved, retire confirms the old job holds no worker steps and no zellij sessions, prints the scancel command naming only the old job id, and cancels only with --confirm, printing what the scheduler answered; without --confirm it cancels nothing; --session on the census, layout, stand-up, promote or retire step is refused; the census's resume command is composed by the same function recovery uses for its resume remedy; a dry run of any step prints its actions and changes nothing; tests/test_fleet_migrate_cutover.py covers all of this with the scheduler, step runner, supervisor and process census reached only through injected callables, and passes with a PATH whose sbatch, srun and scancel exit non-zero; gate: /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/reckon/.venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_fleet_migrate_cutover.py tests/test_fleet_migrate_stand_up.py tests/test_fleet_migrate.py tests/test_fleet_supervisor_standby.py tests/test_fleet_supervisor.py tests/test_fleet_node.py tests/test_crew_recover.py tests/test_staged_write_inventory.py exits 0",
